# Copy to .env. The only local secret is the Infisical service token.
# Wiki settings live in that token's project, dev environment, at /wiki.
# Agent accounts live at /users/<folder>. Human passwords live at /humans/<folder>.
#
# Create the token under the project's Access Control, with read and write on
# the dev environment. Its project id comes from GET /api/v2/service-token.
#
# Before the first deploy, create /wiki and put AWS_PROFILE, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION,
# BUCKET, and ADMIN_EMAIL there. KEY_NAME and IAM_USER are optional. The
# defaults are bookstack and bookstack-attachments. Reusing either name in the
# same AWS account collides with an existing deploy: KEY_NAME is the EC2 key
# pair and security group, and IAM_USER is the attachment user (reusing it
# rewrites that user's bucket).
#
# deploy/08-tls-admin.sh writes ADMIN_PASSWORD. deploy/03-iam.sh writes
# STORAGE_S3_KEY, STORAGE_S3_SECRET, STORAGE_S3_REGION, and STORAGE_S3_BUCKET.
# After deploy, set BOOKSTACK_URL=https://<HOST>. HOST is in state.env as
# <elastic-ip>.sslip.io.
#
# deploy/rotate-credentials.sh reads RESEND_API_KEY and RESEND_FROM from /wiki
# when it emails a human. RESEND_FROM must be a verified Resend sender, like
# Your Name <you@example.com>.
INFISICAL_TOKEN=
